Rules:
  [C1] Use ASP.NET Core for web APIs.
  [C2] Use Entity Framework Core for data access.
  [C3] Use dependency injection.
  [C4] Use repository pattern.
  [C5] Use DTOs for API contracts.
  [C6] Use MediatR for CQRS.
  [C7] Use FluentValidation for validation.
  [C8] Use Serilog for logging.

Pros:
  - Excellent IDE support
  - Strong ecosystem
  - Good performance

Cons:
  - Memory usage
  - Framework complexity
  - Learning curve

Alternatives:
  - Go (simpler)
  - Java (similar)
  - Node.js (lighter)

